@@ -987,3 +987,13 @@ A parallel, additive guard alongside the `did_not_finish` (#1208/#1261) mid-flig
 ### Amendment (2026-10-04, #2271) — nested loops, no backward route
 
 ADR-068 supersedes the rc 11 `route_back` row of this ADR's terminal table. An inner loop that ends without converging ends the outer round when it declares `on_max: halt` or ran out with tests failing (rc 8); the outer loop goes round, each inner loop restarting at round 1. With no outer rounds left, rc 8 still stops the run. A loop may declare `unowned: yield | halt` (ADR-068 §8). Tests: `tests/integration/nested-loop-rounds-test.sh`, `tests/integration/unowned-finding-test.sh`.
+
+### Amendment (2026-10-05, #2032) — generic unfinished-member convergence suppression
+
+A third convergence-suppression case, complementing the `did_not_finish` (#1208/#1261) build-specific guard and the `no_committed_changes` (#1265) guard. When the exit_when predicate fires (`converged==0`) and ANY member of the current iteration carried an unfinished disposition (`timed_out`, `out_of_turns`, or `interrupted`, as determined by `disposition_unfinished`), the cycle must not converge — even for cycles that have no build member (e.g. `design_verify_cycle`).
+
+- **Suppression.** After the build-specific `did_not_finish` check and the `no_committed_changes` check, if `converged==0` AND `_iter_did_not_finish==1`, set `converged=1` and emit `cycle.member_unfinished.suppressed_convergence`. The `converged==0` guard prevents double-fire when the build-specific block already fired.
+- **Empty-diff resting point exempt.** An `empty_diff` stall has all members at `disposition:complete`, so `_iter_did_not_finish==0` and this block never fires.
+- **Max-iterations boundary.** When suppression fires on the last iteration, `converged=1` and the max-iterations path takes over; for cycles without a test member (`_exh_tests_reported==0`), the existing `#1261` exhaustion path emits `cycle.timeout_exhausted` with `reason=design_timeout_exhausted` and `term_rc=8`.
+- **Event registered.** `cycle.member_unfinished.suppressed_convergence` is in `config/event-schema.json`.
+- **Tests.** `tests/integration/cycle-member-unfinished-no-convergence-test.sh` SPEC-1 (suppression fires), SPEC-2 (positive baseline — no suppression on all-complete), SPEC-6 (max-iterations exhaustion with unfinished member).
